## Work tracking (TAOS)

Work in this repository is tracked by an operating layer at:

```
{{taos_home}}
```

Use the full command prefix below for all TAOS commands. Keep the quotes
and `--home` argument as printed, including after entering a task worktree.
If the client did not show TAOS status at startup, run:

```bash
{{taos_cli}} status --compact
```

Read `AGENTS.md` in the OS home above for the full contract. List tasks,
then replace `{{prefix}}-N` with the task ID and `codex` with your registered
agent name.

```bash
{{taos_cli}} task list
{{taos_cli}} start --agent codex --task {{prefix}}-N --session "{{prefix}}-N | short label"
```

Read the capsule before following the printed branch or worktree commands.
Use `claim check` with the same command prefix
before writing in an area another agent may hold.

If the project has no check yet, propose one to the person running it. From the
configured project, `{{taos_cli}} use . --json` lists any `suggested_checks`.
